    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization on owner creation for the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` pipeline, following the project's function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` \u2014 reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Val`, strips every non-digit character (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`), requires exactly 10 digits, mutates the DTO in place with the normalized value (so `BuildOwner` maps and stores the 10-digit form), and throws a checked `InvalidTelephoneException` otherwise.\n- `InvalidTelephoneException.java` \u2014 checked exception for the reject case.\n- `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 escalation handler responding `400 Bad Request`.\n- `escalation/...InvalidTelephoneException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `normalizeTelephone` step between `validate` and `build`. It runs after required-field validation (so a blank telephone still yields the missing-fields 400) and before the DTO is mapped/saved, so the stored and returned `telephone` is the 10-digit value.\n\n**Results:** `coreStripsToTenDigits` (`\"(04) 1234-5678\"` \u2192 stored/returned `\"0412345678\"`) and `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` (`\"12345\"` \u2192 400) both pass; full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
